by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-03T07:33:15Z

Follow-up: `GroupSequence::$cascadedGroup` is removed in this PR, since we ended up looking at it while settling the naming.

It was introduced on 2014-02-17 in `a6ed4cae5da`, the node-traverser prototype, where it was really used:

```php
// NodeTraverser
$node->groups[$key]->cascadedGroup = Constraint::DEFAULT_GROUP;

// NodeValidator
array($groupInSequence),
array($groupSequence->cascadedGroup ?: $groupInSequence)
```

That architecture was replaced before 2.5 shipped, and `RecursiveContextualValidator` has passed the same value as a method parameter ever since, computing it itself as `$defaultOverridden ? DEFAULT_GROUP : null`. The property has not been read since. It survived because the local variable kept the same name, so nothing ever flagged it as dead.

No deprecation: since 7.4 typed it without a default, reading it throws `must not be accessed before initialization`, so nothing that works today can be relying on the value. `UPGRADE-8.2.md` records it as a BC break anyway, because assigning to it does not throw and someone could be doing that to no effect.

This also removes the reason I raised naming: `cascadeCurrentGroup` no longer sits next to a near-identical `cascadedGroup`, and it is the only such option on the class now. Nothing to rename on either side.

